── Section 4: Throughput vs Latency Tradeoff ──

  Increasing batch size improves THROUGHPUT (tokens/sec across all requests)
  because the GPU is better utilized. But it also increases TTFT for each
  individual request, because requests must wait for others in the batch.

  This is the fundamental tradeoff in LLM serving:
    Small batch → low latency, low GPU utilization
    Large batch → high GPU utilization, high latency

  The optimal operating point depends on your SLO:
    • Latency-sensitive API: keep batch small (TTFT < 200ms)
    • Throughput-maximising offline: use large batch (maximise tok/s)

  Here we simulate a simple queueing model.

  Requests=64, prefill=50ms/req, decode=2ms/tok, 100 tokens

   Batch    Throughput    P50 TTFT    P99 TTFT     P50 E2E
  ──────  ────────────  ──────────  ──────────  ──────────
       1         400/s          50          50         250
       4        1000/s         200         200         400
       8        1333/s         400         400         600
      16        1600/s         800         800        1000
      32        1778/s        1600        1600        1800

  Throughput: 400 → 1778 tok/s  (batch 1 → 32)
  P99 TTFT:  50 → 1600 ms  (latency penalty)
  ✓ Section 4 passed — larger batch trades latency for throughput

